A||N||6||FIERO1985||Shift Knob Thread Pitch||||1||
Z||000000||FIERO1985||03-11-2001||05:29 PM||||What is a fieros manual thread pitch and then what are most aftermarket pitches and does anyone do re-threading ??<P>Thanks<BR>Dan<BR><P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-11-2001||09:27 PM||||16mm by 1.5mm pitch.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008507.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008507.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||03-12-2001||12:34 AM||||And, no, most aftermarket shift knobs, etc. are made for about a 12mm shaft, so they won't work.<P>||||reg||13
Z||000003||Rodney||03-12-2001||08:40 AM||||I have a new shifter that has a 1/2" diameter shaft. It has no threads and is intended for aftermarket knobs that have set screws. Many aftermarket shift knobs do have set screws so no threads are needed. Includes a leather boot on a steel frame. Basically the same as my Comp Shifter. Just a thinner shaft and no threads. Same price.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||03-12-2001||09:46 AM||||Find a buddy with a drill press.  Get the knob you like, drill it and tap it.  It's not hard.  I clamped mine down with the vise on the press protected with cloth covered wood to keep it from getting scratched.  I lined the smaller hole up in the knob with a drill bit that barely fit down in it so I would drill a nice straight hole when I put the larger bit in. (My two¢ tip of the day.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000005||Formula88||03-12-2001||09:51 AM||||Actually, my problem is finding the proper die to cut threads in the factory diameter shaft so I can reuse my factory shift knob on a custom shifter.  Most places don't carry anything bigger than a 12mm die.||||reg||6
Z||000006||stsmithgt||03-12-2001||11:48 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.consource.com/communities/profile/1697/1674" TARGET=_blank>http://www.consource.com/communities/profile/1697/1674</A>  <BR>I think I got this right.  I looked under taps and dies manufacturing companies in NC through ConSource.com and came up with these guys if you can't easily find one, maybe they might have one available or know where to get one.?||||reg||1
